  "limitations": [
    "Candidate source is a sanitized export of SpaceApp source 6377b5b491 on top of the published 1.1.2, plus four public-repository fixes found by this devtest: core/browser image size budgets, the CLI image mapping of the default room project /opt/spaceapp to /etc, the OpenCode pane starting even when the first-run free-model check fails, and the gateway OAuth client overlay.",
    "VM hosts are x86_64. ARM64 container validation remains a release workflow gate.",
    "Fresh installer timings use preloaded local candidate images; they exclude network image downloads.",
    "Linux runner: the root disk was grown from 72 to 82 GiB (fresh install needed 6.5 GiB free). macOS runner: six untagged images of earlier local candidates were removed to free host disk; no tagged image or retained fixture was touched.",
    "Earlier 1.1.3 candidates (e5a2a1d, bb006ad, ae565bb) were superseded during this run; only evidence for 7fd6217 is accepted (superseded evidence is kept under evidence-*-superseded).",
    "Windows desktop commands ran as interactive scheduled tasks in an owned RDP session; this is not keystroke coverage of every wizard prompt.",
    "The lab VMs were shared with the 1.1.2 release session; the Linux runner was shut down once by that session during an earlier 1.1.3 candidate run, which was then repeated.",
    "Profiles ran one VM boot per sequence under a 20 GiB host memory floor: small at 8 GiB/4 CPU, medium at 12 GiB/4 CPU, large at 16 GiB/8 CPU (Docker Desktop/WSL 8 GiB on macOS/Windows for medium and large); every runner was reverted to 8 GiB/4 CPU and its Docker settings restored. Each sequence used a fresh small fixture that was purged afterwards.",
    "macOS 1.1.1 -> 1.1.3 upgrade fixture was seeded with the small profile because the macOS lab disk had about 7 GiB free.",
    "npm next publication, environment approval and latest promotion have not yet completed."
  ]
}
